== Fruit Granita ==

Blend and freeze. To make a fruit granita, combine the @fruit of your choice{4%cups}(finely chopped), @water{1%cup}, and @cane sugar{1/3%cup} into a #blender{} or #food processor{} and blend ~{30%seconds} until smooth. Taste and adjust the sweetness to your liking. Pour the mixture into a rimmed #sheet pan{} or #baking dish{} that's at least 8X12–inches. Place in the #freezer{} for ~{1%hour}.

> You can use watermelon, peaches, strawberries, mixed berries, or oranges.

> You can use a combination of water and juice instead of just water.

Scrape. After an hour, use a metal #fork{} like a rake, scraping through the mixture to break up the ice. Return to the freezer for another ~{30%minutes} to an hour.

Repeat. Continue scraping with a fork through the mixture every 30 minutes to an hour until it is fully frozen and the granita has a fluffy granulated texture. This should take about 2 hours in total if you have a large sheet tray, or longer if you're using a smaller baking dish.

Serve or store. Scrape into a pile and scoop into chilled #serving glasses{} to serve immediately, or scrape into an #airtight container{} and return to the freezer until you're ready to serve. Garnish with @?sliced fruit{for garnish}.

== Coffee Granita ==

For a coffee granita, mix the @brewed coffee{2%cups} with the @cane sugar{1/2%cup} until the sugar is dissolved. Taste and adjust the sweetness to your liking. Pour the mixture into a rimmed sheet pan or baking dish that's at least 8X12–inches. Place in the freezer for ~{1%hour}.

Scrape. After an hour, use a metal fork like a rake, scraping through the mixture to break up the ice. Return to the freezer for another ~{30%minutes} to an hour.

Repeat. Continue scraping with a fork through the mixture every 30 minutes to an hour until it is fully frozen and the granita has a fluffy granulated texture. This should take about 2 hours in total if you have a large sheet tray, or longer if you're using a smaller baking dish.

Serve or store. Scrape into a pile and scoop into chilled serving glasses to serve immediately, or scrape into an airtight container and return to the freezer until you're ready to serve. Garnish with @?coffee beans{for garnish}.